sec("pricing", 8, "Special pricing: pricing tables", "A", "Lower CLA settlement fees for a rep or an individual client. Settlement fee only.", [
  { t: "h3", x: "The rules" },
  { t: "ul", items: [
    "A pricing table has a name, for example \"Marvin's Pricing\".",
    "Only the line Settlement Fee to CLA Title & Escrow can change. Title insurance, endorsements, recording fees, taxes and every other CLA fee never change.",
    "A table holds fee sets. A fee set is a group of states (any mix of MD, VA, DC and FL, or All states) with up to three fees: purchase buyer pays, purchase seller pays and refinance borrower pays.",
    "A blank box means the standard fee. A fee of $0 waives that line, and the line disappears.",
    "A state can be in only one fee set of a table. The All states set is a fallback for any state with no set of its own, and cannot be ticked together with single states.",
    "For a quote in a state, the set that contains the state wins as a whole. If it leaves a line blank, that line is standard, not the All states fee.",
    "Add members to a table by email: a rep, or an individual client. One email can be in only one table. The person does not need an account yet.",
    "Whose fee applies: first the person's own email table, then the assigned rep's table, otherwise standard fees. So a client in their own table beats their rep's table.",
    "Guests always see standard fees. An admin or super admin gets special pricing only if they also work as a rep.",
    "Only admins and super admins can create or edit tables; every change is in the audit log.",
  ] },
  { t: "h3", x: "Create and fill a table" },
  { t: "ol", items: [
    ["Open Admin, then Rep pricing", ""],
    ["Choose New pricing table, type a name, then Create table", ""],
    ["Open the table and choose Add fee set", "Tick states or All states. The standard fee appears beside each box. Fill the boxes you want to change, then Save fee set."],
    ["If a state is already in another set", "The page says so and offers Move to this set."],
    ["Add members", "Type a rep's or client's email and choose Add. Each row shows whether they have an account, their role, and for a client whether they use this table or follow their rep. An email already in another table offers Move to this table."],
    ["Test it", "Sign in as the rep, or one of their clients, and quote a ZIP in a covered state."],
  ] },
  { t: "img", f: "pricing-tables.png", cap: "Pricing tables list (demo data).", alt: "Pricing tables list" },
  { t: "img", f: "pricing-table-detail.png", cap: "One table: fee sets and members.", alt: "Pricing table detail" },
  { t: "img", f: "pricing-fee-set-editor.png", cap: "Editing a fee set: pick states and enter the three fees.", alt: "Fee set editor" },
  { t: "img", f: "pricing-add-member.png", cap: "Adding a member by email.", alt: "Add member" },
  { t: "h3", x: "Worked example (made-up names)" },
  { t: "p", x: "Create \"Marvin's Pricing\" with three fee sets, then add the rep marvin.rep@example.com and the client agent.one@example.com." },
  { t: "table", cols: ["Fee set", "Purchase buyer", "Purchase seller", "Refinance borrower"], rows: [
    ["MD and VA", "$900", "$500", "(blank)"],
    ["FL", "$1,000", "$800", "$0"],
    ["All states", "$950", "$600", "$350"],
  ] },
  { t: "table", cols: ["Quote", "Settlement fee the person pays", "Why"], rows: [
    ["MD purchase, buyer pays", "$900 (standard $1,075)", "The MD and VA set wins"],
    ["MD purchase, seller pays", "$500 (standard $670)", "Same set"],
    ["MD refinance", "$450 (standard)", "The MD and VA set left refinance blank, so it stays standard, not $350"],
    ["FL refinance", "No settlement fee line", "$0 waives it"],
    ["DC purchase, buyer pays", "$950", "No DC set, so All states applies"],
    ["Title insurance, recording fees, taxes, notary and other CLA fees", "Unchanged", "Only the settlement fee can change"],
  ] },
  { t: "p", x: "The rep and any of the rep's clients get these fees. If agent.one@example.com is instead listed in another table, that table beats the rep's table for that client. Remove the client's own email and they follow their rep again." },
  { t: "h3", x: "What people see" },
  { t: "ul", items: [
    "On screen, the CLA fees panel shows the lower amount with \"(special rate, standard $...)\".",
    "On the printed, copied or saved quote only the amount appears, with no word special.",
    "The Seller Net Sheet uses the seller's special settlement fee too.",
    "If anything goes wrong loading pricing, the calculator quietly uses standard fees.",
  ] },
]);

